(1) Phi'' = 4*pi*G*rho_b(x) + f(x)*Derivative(Phi_chi(x), (x, 2)) + Derivative(Phi_chi(x), x)*Derivative(f(x), x) + Derivative(q(x), x)
(1) Phi_chi'' = 4*pi*G*f(x)*rho_b(x) + 4*pi*G*rho_chi(x) - f(x)*Derivative(Phi_chi(x), x)*Derivative(f(x), x) - q(x)*Derivative(f(x), x) + Derivative(Phi(x), x)*Derivative(f(x), x); minus the claimed 4 pi G (rho_chi + f rho_b): (-f(x)*Derivative(Phi_chi(x), x) - q(x) + Derivative(Phi(x), x))*Derivative(f(x), x)  (vanishes only where f' = 0: 0)
(1) constant f: Phi sourced by f**2*rho_b + f*rho_chi + rho_b (baryon-baryon coupling (1 + f^2) G); Phi_chi by f*rho_b + rho_chi
(1) gradient-energy Hessian det 1/(16*pi**2*G**2) > 0 and trace < 0 for all f: no ghost
(2) Psi equation: R_W**2*mu_0*Derivative(Psi(x), (x, 2)) + mu_0*(c_1*rho_chi(x) - Psi(x)) + Derivative(F(Psi(x)), Psi(x))*Derivative(L_g(F(Psi(x))), F(Psi(x))) = 0. Horn A (mu_0 large): a Yukawa self-force >= a_extra; horn B (mu_0 small): Psi is not the Helmholtz field, or momentum is violated by a_extra. No mu_0 escapes.
